.TH FERROR 3
.SH NAME
ferror, feof, clearerr, fileno \- stream status inquiries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <stdio.h>

int
feof(stream)
FILE *stream;

int
ferror(stream)
FILE *stream;

clearerr(stream)
FILE *stream;

int
fileno(stream)
FILE *stream;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B feof
returns nonzero once a read on
.I stream
has come to the end of the file, and 0 until then.
.PP
.B ferror
returns nonzero once a read or write on
.I stream
has failed, and 0 until then.
.PP
The two flags stay set until
.B clearerr
clears them both;
.BR rewind (3)
clears both too, and
.BR fseek (3)
and
.BR ungetc (3)
clear the end of file flag.
.PP
.B fileno
returns the file descriptor of
.IR stream ,
for use with the system calls.
.PP
These are macros.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
	while ((c = getc(fp)) != EOF)
		...
	if (ferror(fp))
		fprintf(stderr, "read error\en");
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
fopen(3), getc(3), fread(3), stdio(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.BR clearerr ,
.BR feof ,
.B ferror
and
.B fileno
functions first appeared in Version 7 AT&T UNIX.
